{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.vCoshSinh_not_barFixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.vCoshSinh_not_barFixed","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.lean#L108-L118","doc":"**The constraint is non-trivial.** The cosh/sinh model is *not* bar-fixed — its Q_β channel is\ngenuinely nonzero away from `η = 0` — so self-duality is a real restriction on fibre objects, not\nan artifact of the class shape (§3b-tax non-degeneracy). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.im_at_classical_point_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.im_at_classical_point_zero","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.lean#L100-L106","doc":"At the bar fixed **point** `η = 0` (the classical point `q = 1`) the Q_β channel of *every*\nfibre object vanishes — no self-duality hypothesis needed. β-decay is a strictly `q ≠ 1`\n(deformation) phenomenon. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.barFixed_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.barFixed_real","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.lean#L92-L98","doc":"On the self-dual locus `𝔙` is **purely real**: the fibre object equals its binding (Re)\nchannel — the bare Higgs contributes only the volume/mass face. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.barFixed_qbeta_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.barFixed_qbeta_zero","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.lean#L84-L90","doc":"**Self-dual locus vanishing (the CS = 0 mechanism, fibre-map instance).** A bar-fixed\ncomplex-volume fibre object has identically vanishing Q_β (bar-odd / imaginary) channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.BarFixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.BarFixed","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.lean#L80-L82","doc":"A fibre object is **bar-fixed** (self-dual / amphichiral source): `V(−η) = V(η)`. This is the\nfibre-map form of `J_N(q) = J_N(q⁻¹)` (the Higgs `4₁` self-duality). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.instComplexVolumeFibreVCoshSinh","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.instComplexVolumeFibreVCoshSinh","kind":"instance","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.lean#L58-L64","doc":"**The conjecture class is non-vacuous.** `V₀(η) = cosh η + i·sinh η` is a complex-volume fibre\nobject: `Re V₀ = cosh η` is bar-even (binding channel) and `Im V₀ = sinh η` is bar-odd (Q_β\nchannel). This witnesses the structural shape is realizable — it does **not** claim the framework's\nobservables descend from `V₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.vCoshSinh_im","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.vCoshSinh_im","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.lean#L54-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.vCoshSinh_re","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.vCoshSinh_re","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.lean#L50-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.vCoshSinh","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.vCoshSinh","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.lean#L47-L48","doc":"The natural `cosh/sinh` model `V₀(η) = cosh η + i·sinh η`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.ComplexVolumeFibre.im_bar_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.ComplexVolumeFibre.im_bar_odd","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.lean#L45-L45","doc":"`Im V` is bar-odd — the Q_β (sinh) channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.ComplexVolumeFibre.re_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.ComplexVolumeFibre.re_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.lean#L43-L43","doc":"`Re V` is bar-even — the binding (cosh) channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.ComplexVolumeFibre.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.ComplexVolumeFibre.mk","kind":"ctor","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.lean#L41-L41","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.ComplexVolumeFibre","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.ComplexVolumeFibre","kind":"class","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.lean#L37-L45","doc":"**conj:binding-qbeta-complex-volume (fibre descent), §3b class.** A complex-volume fibre object\nis a map `V : ℝ → ℂ` whose **real part is bar-even** (binding / cosh channel: even under `η ↦ −η`)\nand **imaginary part is bar-odd** (Q_β / sinh channel: odd under `η ↦ −η`). The framework's binding\nand Q_β observables descending from one such `V` is the open conjecture. ","signatureChunk":0}]}